{"id":"mahabharata-7-109","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":109,"title":"नवाधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 109 · Bhima defeats Karna again","summary":{"en":"Left without a chariot, Karna is again overcome by Bhima, takes another chariot, and Bhima cuts down his banner with two razor arrows. Karna passes a fallen warrior and sighs deeply, and Bhima draws his gilded bow again.","kn":"ರಥವಿಲ್ಲದ ಕರ್ಣ ಮತ್ತೆ ಭೀಮನಿಂದ ಸೋತು ಇನ್ನೊಂದು ರಥ ಏರುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಭೀಮ ಎರಡು ಕ್ಷುರಗಳಿಂದ ಅವನ ಧ್ವಜ ಕಡಿಯುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಬಿದ್ದ ವೀರನನ್ನು ದಾಟಿ ಕರ್ಣ ದೀರ್ಘ ನಿಟ್ಟುಸಿರು ಬಿಡುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಭೀಮ ಮತ್ತೆ ಚಿನ್ನದ ಬಿಲ್ಲು ಎಳೆಯುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"रथहीन कर्ण भीम से फिर पराजित होता है, दूसरा रथ लेता है, और भीम दो क्षुर बाणों से उसका ध्वज काट देते हैं। कर्ण गिरे योद्धा को लाँघकर लम्बी साँस लेता है और भीम फिर स्वर्णमण्डित धनुष खींचते हैं।","te":"రథం లేని కర్ణుడు మళ్లీ భీమునిచే ఓడి మరో రథం ఎక్కుతాడు; భీముడు రెండు క్షురబాణాలతో అతని ధ్వజాన్ని ఛేదిస్తాడు. పడిన వీరుని దాటి కర్ణుడు దీర్ఘంగా నిట్టూరుస్తాడు; భీముడు మళ్లీ బంగారు విల్లు ఎక్కుపెడతాడు.","ta":"தேரிழந்த கர்ணன் மீண்டும் பீமனிடம் தோற்று, வேறு தேரில் ஏற, பீமன் இரு க்ஷுர அம்புகளால் அவன் கொடியை வெட்டுகிறான். வீழ்ந்த வீரனைக் கடந்து கர்ணன் நீண்ட பெருமூச்சு விட, பீமன் பொன் வில்லை மீண்டும் வளைக்கிறான்.","ml":"തേരില്ലാതായ കർണ്ണനെ വീണ്ടും ഭീമൻ തോൽപ്പിക്കുന്നു; അദ്ദേഹം മറ്റൊരു രഥം എടുക്കുന്നു, ഭീമൻ രണ്ട് മൂർച്ചയുള്ള അമ്പുകൊണ്ട് കൊടി മുറിക്കുന്നു. വീണുകിടക്കുന്ന ഒരു യോദ്ധാവിനെ കടന്നുപോകുമ്പോൾ കർണ്ണൻ ദീർഘമായി നെടുവീർപ്പിടുന്നു; ഭീമൻ സ്വർണവില്ല് വീണ്ടും ഉയർത്തുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.109; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"जयद्रथवधपर्व","titleEn":"Jayadrathavadha Parva (Slaying of Jayadratha)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"स तथा विरथः कर्णः पुनर्भीमेन निर्जितः ।\nरथमन्यं समास्थाय सद्यो विव्याध पाण्डवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna, thus made chariotless and beaten again by Bhima, mounted another chariot and at once struck the Pandava."}},{"n":2,"text":"महागजाविवासाद्य विषाणाग्रैः परस्परम् ।\nशरैः पूर्णायतोत्सृष्टैरन्योन्यमभिजघ्नतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like two great elephants closing with the tips of their tusks, they struck each other with arrows drawn to the full and loosed."}},{"n":3,"text":"अथ कर्णः शरव्रातैर्भीमं बलवदर्दयत् ।\nननाद बलवन्नादं पुनर्विव्याध चोरसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Karna tormented Bhima hard with flights of arrows, roared a mighty roar, and struck him again in the chest."}},{"n":4,"text":"तं भीमो दशभिर्बाणैः प्रत्यविध्यदजिह्मगैः ।\nपुनर्विव्याध विंशत्या शराणां नतपर्वणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima struck him back with ten straight-flying arrows, and again with twenty smooth-jointed arrows."}},{"n":5,"text":"कर्णस्तु नवभिर्भीमं विद्ध्वा राजन्स्तनान्तरे ।\nध्वजमेकेन विव्याध सायकेन शितेन ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna, having pierced Bhima between the breasts with nine, O king, struck his banner with one sharp arrow."}},{"n":6,"text":"सायकानां ततः पार्थस्त्रिषष्ट्या प्रत्यविध्यत ।\nतोत्त्रैरिव महानागं कशाभिरिव वाजिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Partha struck back with sixty-three arrows, as one drives a great elephant with goads and a horse with whips."}},{"n":7,"text":"सोऽतिविद्धो महाराज पाण्डवेन यशस्विना ।\nसृक्विणी लेलिहन्वीरः क्रोधसंरक्तलोचनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Deeply wounded by the glorious Pandava, great king, the hero licked the corners of his mouth, his eyes red with anger."}},{"n":8,"text":"ततः शरं महाराज सर्वकायावदारणम् ।\nप्राहिणोद्भीमसेनाय बलायेन्द्र इवाशनिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, great king, he sent at Bhimasena an arrow that would split the whole body, as Indra hurls the thunderbolt at Bala."}},{"n":9,"text":"स निर्भिद्य रणे पार्थं सूतपुत्रधनुश्च्युतः ।\nअगच्छद्दारयन्भूमिं चित्रपुङ्खः शिलीमुखः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shot from the charioteer's son's bow, that arrow with bright feathers and a keen head pierced Partha in the fight and went on tearing into the earth."}},{"n":10,"text":"सर्वशैक्यां चतुष्किष्कुं गुर्वीं रुक्माङ्गदां गदाम् ।\nप्राहिणोत्सूतपुत्राय षडस्रामविचारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima, without hesitation, hurled at the charioteer's son a heavy mace, wholly of iron, four cubits long, with gold armlets and six faces."}},{"n":11,"text":"तया जघानाधिरथेः सदश्वान्साधुवाहिनः ।\nगदया भारतः क्रुद्धो वज्रेणेन्द्र इवासुरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With that mace the enraged Bharata killed Adhiratha's son's fine, well-drawing horses, as Indra with the thunderbolt kills asuras."}},{"n":12,"text":"ततो भीमो महाबाहुः क्षुराभ्यां भरतर्षभ ।\nध्वजमाधिरथेश्छित्त्वा सूतमभ्यहनत्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then mighty-armed Bhima, best of the Bharatas, with two razor-edged arrows cut down the banner of Adhiratha's son and killed his charioteer."}},{"n":13,"text":"हताश्वसूतमुत्सृज्य रथं स पतितध्वजम् ।\nविस्फारयन्धनुः कर्णस्तस्थौ भारत दुर्मनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Leaving the chariot with its horses and charioteer slain and its banner down, Karna stood, O Bharata, flexing his bow, in low spirits."}},{"n":14,"text":"तत्राद्भुतमपश्याम राधेयस्य पराक्रमम् ।\nविरथो रथिनां श्रेष्ठो वारयामास यद्रिपुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There we saw a marvel of Radheya's prowess: chariotless, that best of chariot-fighters held back his enemy."}},{"n":15,"text":"विरथं तं रथश्रेष्ठं दृष्ट्वाधिरथिमाहवे ।\nदुर्योधनस्ततो राजन्नभ्यभाषत दुर्मुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the best of chariot-fighters, Adhiratha's son, chariotless in the battle, King Duryodhana then spoke to Durmukha, O king."}},{"n":16,"text":"एष दुर्मुख राधेयो भीमेन विरथीकृतः ।\nतं रथेन नरश्रेष्ठं संपादय महारथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Durmukha, Radheya has been made chariotless by Bhima. Provide a chariot for that best of men, the great chariot-warrior.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"दुर्योधनवचः श्रुत्वा ततो भारत दुर्मुखः ।\nत्वरमाणोऽभ्ययात्कर्णं भीमं चावारयच्छरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing Duryodhana's words, Durmukha, O Bharata, hurried to Karna and held Bhima back with arrows."}},{"n":18,"text":"दुर्मुखं प्रेक्ष्य संग्रामे सूतपुत्रपदानुगम् ।\nवायुपुत्रः प्रहृष्टोऽभूत्सृक्किणी परिलेलिहन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Durmukha in the battle following the charioteer's son's footsteps, the son of the Wind was delighted, licking the corners of his mouth."}},{"n":19,"text":"ततः कर्णं महाराज वारयित्वा शिलीमुखैः ।\nदुर्मुखाय रथं शीघ्रं प्रेषयामास पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, great king, the Pandava, holding Karna back with arrows, swiftly turned his chariot toward Durmukha."}},{"n":20,"text":"तस्मिन्क्षणे महाराज नवभिर्नतपर्वभिः ।\nसुपुङ्खैर्दुर्मुखं भीमः शरैर्निन्ये यमक्षयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In that instant, great king, Bhima sent Durmukha to Yama's abode with nine well-feathered, smooth-jointed arrows."}},{"n":21,"text":"ततस्तमेवाधिरथिः स्यन्दनं दुर्मुखे हते ।\nआस्थितः प्रबभौ राजन्दीप्यमान इवांशुमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"After Durmukha was slain, Adhiratha's son, mounting that same chariot, shone, O king, like the blazing sun."}},{"n":22,"text":"शयानं भिन्नमर्माणं दुर्मुखं शोणितोक्षितम् ।\nदृष्ट्वा कर्णोऽश्रुपूर्णाक्षो मुहूर्तं नाभ्यवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Durmukha lying with his vital parts broken and drenched in blood, Karna, his eyes full of tears, for a moment did not move."}},{"n":23,"text":"तं गतासुमतिक्रम्य कृत्वा कर्णः प्रदक्षिणम् ।\nदीर्घमुष्णं श्वसन्वीरो न किंचित्प्रत्यपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"He passed the lifeless body, circling it with his right side toward it, and the hero, sighing long and hot, did nothing."}},{"n":24,"text":"तस्मिंस्तु विवरे राजन्नाराचान्गार्ध्रवाससः ।\nप्राहिणोत्सूतपुत्राय भीमसेनश्चतुर्दश ॥","meaning":{"en":"In that opening, O king, Bhimasena sent fourteen nitaracha arrows with vulture feathers at the charioteer's son."}},{"n":25,"text":"ते तस्य कवचं भित्त्वा स्वर्णपुङ्खा महौजसः ।\nहेमचित्रा महाराज द्योतयन्तो दिशो दश ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those gold-feathered, very powerful arrows, painted with gold, great king, pierced his armor, lighting the ten directions."}},{"n":26,"text":"अपिबन्सूतपुत्रस्य शोणितं रक्तभोजनाः ।\nक्रुद्धा इव मनुष्येन्द्र भुजगाः कालचोदिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Feeding on blood, they drank the charioteer's son's blood, like angry snakes driven by Death, lord of men."}},{"n":27,"text":"प्रसर्पमाणा मेदिन्यां ते व्यरोचन्त मार्गणाः ।\nअर्धप्रविष्टाः संरब्धा बिलानीव महोरगाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Creeping into the earth, those arrows shone, half entered, furious, like great serpents going into holes."}},{"n":28,"text":"तं प्रत्यविध्यद्राधेयो जाम्बूनदविभूषितैः ।\nचतुर्दशभिरत्युग्रैर्नाराचैरविचारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Radheya struck him back without hesitation with fourteen very fierce nitarachas adorned with Jambunada gold."}},{"n":29,"text":"ते भीमसेनस्य भुजं सव्यं निर्भिद्य पत्रिणः ।\nप्राविशन्मेदिनीं भीमाः क्रौञ्चं पत्ररथा इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those feathered arrows, terrible, pierced Bhimasena's left arm and entered the earth, as herons' flight enters a Krauncha mountain."}},{"n":30,"text":"ते व्यरोचन्त नाराचाः प्रविशन्तो वसुंधराम् ।\nगच्छत्यस्तं दिनकरे दीप्यमाना इवांशवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those nitarachas shone as they entered the earth, like blazing rays when the sun is setting."}},{"n":31,"text":"स निर्भिन्नो रणे भीमो नाराचैर्मर्मभेदिभिः ।\nसुस्राव रुधिरं भूरि पर्वतः सलिलं यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pierced in the battle by the nitarachas that break vital parts, Bhima bled much, as a mountain gives forth water."}},{"n":32,"text":"स भीमस्त्रिभिरायस्तः सूतपुत्रं पतत्रिभिः ।\nसुपर्णवेगैर्विव्याध सारथिं चास्य सप्तभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima, steady, struck the charioteer's son with three arrows swift as Garuda, and his charioteer with seven."}},{"n":33,"text":"स विह्वलो महाराज कर्णो भीमबलार्दितः ।\nप्राद्रवज्जवनैरश्वै रणं हित्वा महायशाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Distressed, great king, and tormented by Bhima's strength, the greatly renowned Karna left the battle and fled with his swift horses."}},{"n":34,"text":"भीमसेनस्तु विस्फार्य चापं हेमपरिष्कृतम् ।\nआहवेऽतिरथोऽतिष्ठज्ज्वलन्निव हुताशनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Bhimasena, flexing his gold-adorned bow, stood in the battle, an atiratha, blazing like a fire."}}]}]}